Hello,

At the moment, there is no way to turn it off from poppr itself, but there are a couple of things you can do:

1. you can copy and modify the internal boot_plot() function <https://github.com/grunwaldlab/poppr/blob/94c745aa2e6a806a125f48b86f9c07d8b6ec95aa/R/internal.r#L2070-L2107> to not display the points and then plot it using the "raw" output of diversity_ci() (here's how it is used in the code <https://github.com/grunwaldlab/poppr/blob/94c745aa2e6a806a125f48b86f9c07d8b6ec95aa/R/bootstraping.R#L682-L688>).
2. you can modify the components of the ggplot2 object

Best,
Zhian

